      "data": {
        "delta": "**First, confirm your entry route with ICP**, since entry rules depend on nationality. In parallel, start your company preparation and family paperwork.\n\n**Before you land:**\n- **Company:** choose the jurisdiction, then the licensed business activity and bankability pre-check, then trade-name reservation and initial approval. Your path places these before arrival; confirm remote procedures with ADDED or the relevant free-zone authority.\n- **Family:** start marriage and birth certificate attestation with your home-country authority and UAE MOFA. The path’s likely duration is **21 days**, so start early.\n- **School:** begin applications to ADEK-licensed schools after the attestation step. Final enrolment typically needs your child’s Emirates ID; confirm requirements with the school.\n\n**After landing:** arrange temporary accommodation, a local mobile number and founder health insurance. Following trade-name approval, your path schedules the office/flexi-desk lease and constitutional documents in parallel; both precede the commercial licence.\n\nThese are planning steps, not confirmed approvals. Several source entries have low confidence and require authority verification.",
        "verified": true
      }
